  "published": "2025-11-15T13:38:26.35Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- v5.0.0 rewrites the API surface as extension members on `System.Console`, introduces `WriteInterpolated`/`WriteLineInterpolated`, and exposes helpers such as `Selection`, `Menu`, `Table`, `ReadLine`, and `TryReadLine` directly on the console.\n\t\t\t- `ColoredOutput` and the `Color` struct were removed; styling now flows through the enhanced `ConsoleColor` helpers (`DefaultForeground`, `DefaultBackground`, `Default`, and `/` tuples) together with the interpolated string handler to keep colored output allocation-free.\n\t\t\t- `ProgressBar` and `IndeterminateProgressBar` are standalone types, and `ProgressBar.WriteProgressBar` plus the instance helper now accept an optional `maxLineWidth` for constrained layouts.\n\t\t\t- New utilities include `TextWriter.WriteWhiteSpaces(int)` for allocation-free padding, `Markup` for ANSI decorations that collapse when output is redirected, and formatting shortcuts such as `duration` (for `TimeSpan`) and `bytes` (for `double`) on `PrettyConsoleInterpolatedStringHandler`.",
